user: Finish the existing Daylight task board. Inspect its current files, repair preview persistence using the configured asynchronous artifact storage, and preserve its polished responsive design. Add, edit, delete, completion, All/Active/Completed filtering, empty state, and task counts must work. Build a fresh artifact and verify those behaviors with concrete interaction assertions, including editing and a reload that retains the changed task. Read the current tool descriptions and response contract, use the selected Local Bun workspace, and keep repairing until the delivered revision passes.

## RESPONSE FORMAT

Reply in TOON: one `field: value` per block, blank line between blocks.
List values use bracket notation [item one, item two].
No markdown fences, no bold, no bullets, no other field names.

- thoughts (list): your reasoning, one step per item
- observations (list): what the last result told you
- do (text): exactly 'tool' to run tools, or 'done' to reply — never a tool name, tool names belong in act
- act (tool calls, or text): what do asked for. With 'tool', the tools to run, each written as name({"key": "value"}) and grouped [[first, second], [third]] — those in the same inner list run at the same time, the lists run one after another. With 'done', the reply, in plain words. One or the other, never both.

### Example

thoughts: [item one, item two]

observations: [item one, item two]

do: <do>

act: [[first({"key": "value"}), second({"key": "value"})]] — or the reply itself, when do is done

